  {
    "episode_id": 84037,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84037.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "Mr. President, we've in recent weeks had more information about the targeting of General Flynn, about the lies and the conspiracy around the Russia gate or Obama gate and these different versions of essentially the Russia-Russia conspiracy. I wanted to know what we should be expecting going forward. Are there more revelations? I mean, Director of National Intelligence acting now departed. Richard Grinnell did a fantastic job from a transparency perspective. Are we getting at more transparency? Because the American people deserve to know what was done to you and what happened to your administration before we go in and look at the next possible election.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The American public deserves to know what was done to the President and what happened to his administration.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "In recent weeks, there has been more information about the targeting of General Flynn.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The Director of National Intelligence has recently departed.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "There have been lies and conspiracies surrounding the Russia gate or Obama gate narratives.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Multiple versions of a 'Russia-Russia' conspiracy exist.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Richard Grinnell performed excellently in terms of transparency during his tenure.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The President is personally affected by the events described and sees himself as a victim of political targeting.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Transparency is a legitimate and necessary standard for evaluating government conduct.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The term 'Russia-Russia conspiracy' implies internal Russian collusion rather than foreign interference, which suggests a specific interpretation of the original narrative.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Public awareness of past actions will inform judgment on future elections.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The departure of the Director of National Intelligence signals a shift in policy direction related to disclosure.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Topic Shift"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 84037,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84037.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "It should never be allowed to happen again, Buck. What happened to this administration? What happened to General Flynn? What happened to others that are going through it still? It was an attempted coup. It was an attempted takedown of a duly elected president. It happened to be me. It could have been anybody. But you would think we're not a third world country. This was a a coup, and they got caught, and they've been caught. I think John Ratcliffe is going to do a fantastic job. Bill Barr is doing a terrific job. And I specifically, as you know, I mean, you know it probably better than anybody. I would absolutely have the right to totally get involved. I've chosen not to, because I think it's better that if I didn't, I could, and I could have, but I've chosen not to, Bill Barr's handling it. Other people are handling it. John Ratcliffe now is fantastic. He'll be involved. But I will say this, I believe you're going to see things that will shock the minds, even of the people that were most skeptical. It is incredible. I think it's the greatest scandal, political scandal, certainly in the history of our country. This makes Watergate what they did to us, many of us, but what they did to this country makes Watergate look like small potatoes.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "It should never be allowed to happen again.",
        "confidence": 0.97
